# DRAFT — NOT ENABLED. This file deliberately ends in `.disabled` so GitHub
# never registers it as a workflow. Renaming it to `.yml` is the act of turning
# it on, and that is a decision for a human, not a side effect of a merge.
#
# What this would do
# ------------------
# Run `scripts/catalogue_gridatlas_v9.py refresh-composition`, which rewrites the
# four identity fields of the one catalogue row bracketed by the
# GRIDATLAS_V9_AUTOMATION markers — the version in `name:`, the
# `CURRENT VERIFIED · v… · … ·` prefix of `note:`, `data_gridatlas_release:` and
# the trailing HTML comment — so the public homepage stops silently drifting
# behind the live Grid Atlas composition. It carries the human-written
# measurement prose in `note:` through byte for byte; it does not write that text
# and must never be given the job of writing it.
#
# Why it is off
# -------------
# The homepage is the public front door. The compiler was unjammed on the same
# night this draft was written, and one green run against one input is not
# evidence that an unattended run is safe.
#
# What would have to be true before anyone turns it on
# ----------------------------------------------------
#  1. The refresh has been run by hand, by a person who read the diff, on at
#     least three separate composition generations, and each time changed
#     exactly one line. One proof (v9.98 -> v9.99, 2026-09-04) exists so far.
#
#  2. SATISFIED (2026-09-04). `scripts/test_catalogue_gridatlas_v9.py` pins the
#     fail-closed cases against a fixture that reproduces the three-way href
#     collision, so a later edit cannot quietly relax them. It is dependency-free
#     and is run as a step below. Twenty checks, including the one that matters:
#     a banner carrying the same href must be ACCEPTED.
#
#  3. The upstream pointers are consistent again. As of 2026-09-04 they are not,
#     and this is the deeper defect: `catalogue-gridatlas-v9.yml` asserts
#     `cmp current-v3.json live-set.json`, but those two files differ at char 2
#     of line 1 and carry different schemas. That workflow therefore cannot reach
#     the compiler at all, and `releases/current-v3.json` is still frozen at the
#     202608291430 immutable-release model while the site has moved to the
#     composition model. Automating a second workflow on top of an upstream that
#     is already inconsistent would hide the inconsistency, not fix it.
#
#  4. A human-review gate exists on the resulting commit. The current governance
#     is that nothing reaches `main` unreviewed; this workflow pushes to `main`,
#     so it contradicts that rule until the rule changes or the workflow is
#     changed to open a pull request instead.
#
#  5. Concurrency with the Pages deployment is settled. This shares
#     `concurrency: pages` with `catalogue-gridatlas-v9.yml`; two publishers
#     racing for one homepage is how a snapshot gets overwritten.
#
#  6. Someone owns the note. The refresher moves the four identity fields but
#     cannot write the measurement prose in `note:`, so an unattended run would
#     otherwise leave the row naming v10.02 while the note still argues v9.99's
#     case — the nine-release drift inverted. The compiler now flags that
#     instead: it prefixes the note with `notes written for v9.99 · `, in plain
#     English because `note:` is rendered publicly and a reader is owed the fact
#     that the argument describes an earlier build. The flag is NOT a licence to
#     run unattended forever — a second refresh while it still stands is a hard
#     refusal, which bounds the drift at exactly one generation. So before this
#     is enabled, a named person must be on the hook to rewrite the note within
#     one generation, and `--notes-current` (which clears the flag) must never be
#     passed by this workflow: a machine cannot know that the prose is current.
#
# Until all six hold, run it locally and read the diff:
#
#   python scripts/catalogue_gridatlas_v9.py refresh-composition \
#     --root . --gridatlas ../gridatlas --check

name: Refresh Grid Atlas composition row (DRAFT, DISABLED)
run-name: Refresh the marked Grid Atlas catalogue row from the live composition

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      expected_composition_generation:
        description: Fail closed unless the live composition is this generation
        required: true
        type: string
      apply:
        description: Write and commit the refresh (false = report the diff only)
        required: true
        default: false
        type: boolean

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: pages
  cancel-in-progress: false

env:
  GRIDATLAS_REPOSITORY: Ventusltd/gridatlas

jobs:
  refresh:
    name: Refresh the marked catalogue row and prove one line changed
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 10
    permissions:
      contents: write
    steps:
      - name: Checkout GlobalGrid main
        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262
        with:
          ref: main
          fetch-depth: 1

      - name: Check out the pinned Grid Atlas commit
        id: upstream
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          commit="$(timeout 30 git ls-remote "https://github.com/${GRIDATLAS_REPOSITORY}.git" refs/heads/main | awk 'NR == 1 { print $1 }')"
          [[ "$commit" =~ ^[0-9a-f]{40}$ ]]
          git clone --quiet --filter=blob:none --no-checkout \
            "https://github.com/${GRIDATLAS_REPOSITORY}.git" "$RUNNER_TEMP/gridatlas"
          git -C "$RUNNER_TEMP/gridatlas" checkout --quiet "$commit"
          echo "commit=$commit" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"

      - name: Set up Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@a26af69be951a213d495a4c3e4e4022e16d87065
        with:
          python-version: '3.12'

      - name: Refuse a composition generation the operator did not expect
        env:
          GRIDATLAS_DIR: ${{ runner.temp }}/gridatlas
          EXPECTED: ${{ inputs.expected_composition_generation }}
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          observed="$(jq -er '.current.atlas_composition.generation' "$GRIDATLAS_DIR/state/live-set.json")"
          [[ "$observed" == "$EXPECTED" ]] || {
            echo "Live composition is ${observed}, operator expected ${EXPECTED}; refusing" >&2
            exit 1
          }

      - name: Prove the live composition is actually served before naming it
        env:
          GRIDATLAS_DIR: ${{ runner.temp }}/gridatlas
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          manifest="$(jq -er '.current.atlas_composition.manifest' "$GRIDATLAS_DIR/state/live-set.json")"
          generation="$(jq -er '.current.atlas_composition.generation' "$GRIDATLAS_DIR/state/live-set.json")"
          curl --fail --silent --show-error --location --retry 3 --max-time 30 \
            "https://ventusltd.github.io/gridatlas/${manifest#atlas/}" -o "$RUNNER_TEMP/live-composition.json" \
            || curl --fail --silent --show-error --location --retry 3 --max-time 30 \
                 "https://ventusltd.github.io/gridatlas/${manifest}" -o "$RUNNER_TEMP/live-composition.json"
          [[ "$(jq -er '.generation' "$RUNNER_TEMP/live-composition.json")" == "$generation" ]]

      - name: Pin the fail-closed contracts before touching the homepage
        shell: bash
        run: python3 scripts/test_catalogue_gridatlas_v9.py

      - name: Refresh the marked row
        env:
          GRIDATLAS_DIR: ${{ runner.temp }}/gridatlas
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          # --notes-current is deliberately NOT passed: only a human who wrote
          # the measurement prose may assert it describes the incoming release.
          python3 scripts/catalogue_gridatlas_v9.py refresh-composition \
            --root . --gridatlas "$GRIDATLAS_DIR" \
            --result-json "$RUNNER_TEMP/refresh.json"
          cat "$RUNNER_TEMP/refresh.json"
          if [[ "$(jq -r '.editorial_lag // "null"' "$RUNNER_TEMP/refresh.json")" != "null" ]]; then
            echo "::warning::The note now lags the identity. A human must rewrite it before the next generation, or the next run will refuse."
          fi

      - name: Assert exactly one line of exactly one file changed
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          changed="$(git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all | cut -c4-)"
          [[ "$changed" == "index.html" || -z "$changed" ]] || {
            echo "Refusing: files other than index.html changed:" >&2
            echo "$changed" >&2
            exit 1
          }
          if [[ -n "$changed" ]]; then
            added="$(git diff --numstat -- index.html | cut -f1)"
            removed="$(git diff --numstat -- index.html | cut -f2)"
            [[ "$added" == "1" && "$removed" == "1" ]] || {
              echo "Refusing: expected one line changed, got +${added}/-${removed}" >&2
              git diff -- index.html >&2
              exit 1
            }
          fi
          git diff -- index.html

      - name: Publication truth gate
        shell: bash
        run: python3 scripts/verify_published_versions.py

      # NOTE: no snapshot step exists here yet. The homepage protocol requires a
      # numbered homepage_versions/homepage_v0NN.html restore point and a README
      # section recorded BEFORE the edit. Until that is automated and proven,
      # this workflow must not be allowed to commit — which is condition 1 above.
      - name: Commit the refresh
        if: ${{ inputs.apply }}
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          echo "Deliberately not implemented in the draft." >&2
          echo "See conditions 1-5 in the header of this file." >&2
          exit 1
